{
  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed nursery, by reason of its overall scale, intensity of use, and the number of children (up to 120) and staff (up to 36) on site for long operating hours throughout the week, would generate significant noise from internal activities, external play areas, and associated comings and goings. In addition, the absence of sufficient on-site parking would result in increased vehicle movements and overspill parking in surrounding residential streets, leading to congestion, parking stress, obstruction of accesses, and further disturbance to neighbouring occupiers. These combined impacts would be concentrated during peak periods but experienced on a daily and sustained basis, resulting in unacceptable harm to the living conditions of nearby residents. Such impacts cannot be adequately mitigated by planning condition. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policy D14, Enfield Core Strategy Policies CP30 and CP32 and Policies DMD16, DMD18, and DMD68 of the Enfield Development Management Document.",
    "The proposed development would generate a significant concentration of vehicle movements during peak nursery drop-off and pick-up periods. The on-site parking provision is insufficient to meet demand, and the surrounding highway network has limited capacity to accommodate overspill parking. Insufficient survey evidence and trip analysis has been provided to demonstrate that the development could operate safely. As a result, the development would be likely to cause congestion, on-street parking pressure, and conflict with other highway users, including pedestrians, resulting in unacceptable impacts on highway safety. The proposal is therefore contrary to  London Plan Policies T4, and T6, Enfield Core Strategy Policies CP25 and CP30 and  Policies DMD37, DMD16 and DMD18 of the Enfield Development Management Document.\r"
  ],
